-- title:
--   Unique natural extension of a family on connected Noetherian test algebras
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ that is a domain of characteristic zero, with $\pi \in \mathcal O$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ $\pi$-adically complete, residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ of cardinality $r$, and $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$; let $K_0$ be a fraction field of $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero. Let $Onr$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra which is a domain of characteristic zero, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo that ideal and every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo it. Let $G$ be a type and let $f_N : N \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ be an arbitrary morphism of schemes. Consider the functor on $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ sending $B$ to $((Onr \to_{\mathcal O} B) \times \mathrm{DeligneDatum}(K_0,\pi,B)) \times G$, where a Deligne datum assigns to each full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M \subset K_0^2$ a $B$-submodule of $B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$ with invertible quotient, compatibly with inclusions of lattices and with homotheties, and satisfying the stated nondegeneracy condition at every prime of $B$; the $G$-factor is constant and the $Onr$-factor is corepresented by $Onr$. Its target is the functor sending $B$ to the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} B \to N$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. Suppose given $u$ assigning to every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent and whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$ a map between these sets, natural for $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphisms between such algebras. Then there is exactly one family $U$, defined for all $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with the image of $\pi$ nilpotent (no Noetherian or idempotent hypothesis), natural for all $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphisms between such, and agreeing with $u$ on Noetherian $B$ with only trivial idempotents.
--
--   This is the extension step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison: a natural transformation from the rigidified Deligne-datum functor, decorated by an inert parameter set $G$, into the functor of $\pi$-nilpotent points of an $\mathcal O$-scheme $N$ is determined by, and can be recovered from, its values on Noetherian test algebras with connected spectrum. It is the form used by the construction of equivariant fine families over the Čerednik–Drinfeld moduli problem.
